From 8d9009c4d1dc86830872b5910b4f90e142b02a59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Barth <dbarth4@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:41:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: make the Fluent list formatter work without ICU

DO NOT MERGE. The code change is complete and correct; the build plumbing
is not. See the last paragraph.

`rustc_error_messages` links `icu_list`, `icu_locale` and the baked ICU data
to format one thing: the Fluent `STRLIST` values in diagnostics such as
"unused imports: `a`, `b`, and `c`". That drags in the whole ICU data model --
`icu_provider`, `yoke`, `zerovec`, `zerofrom`, `tinystr` -- for a list
separator.

Add an `icu` feature gating the three dependencies, with a fallback that
formats lists the English way. The fallback is byte-for-byte what
`ListFormatter` produces for `en`, which is both the locale rustc ships
messages for and the one it already falls back to when the requested locale
is unknown. Verified identical output with the feature on and off for lists
of two, three and four items.

Bootstrap gains `rust.icu` (default true) and enables the feature the way
`rust.debug-logging` enables `max_level_info`.

Measured on a stage1 `librustc_driver` for aarch64-apple-darwin, `strip -x`ed:
111,360,864 -> 110,682,584 bytes, -678,280.

What blocks this: `x build compiler` runs two `Mode::Rustc` cargo
invocations, one over `-p <every compiler crate>` with
`--features "llvm rustc max_level_info"` and one over bare `rustc-main` with
`--features "llvm max_level_info"`. In the first, `rustc_error_messages` is a
selected root package, so a feature on it applies directly; in the second it
is only reached transitively. Giving it any feature at all makes the two
invocations resolve it to two distinct units, and every crate downstream of
it -- almost the whole compiler -- is built twice. Both copies are placed in
the same stage sysroot, so `rustdoc`, `clippy`, `miri` and
`error_index_generator` then fail with E0464, multiple candidates. This
happens with `rust.icu` left at its default as well as switched off.

Both feature mechanisms were tried and both double the build: a `default`
feature dropped with `--no-default-features`, and an additive feature pushed
from `rustc_features`. On an unpatched tree each compiler crate is compiled
once; with either version of this patch, twice. Gating a crate this deep in
the graph needs bootstrap to build the compiler through one cargo invocation,
which is out of scope here.
